n/S1212","line":42},{"title":"initial version","target":"https://legislature.idaho.gov/sessioninfo/2025/legislation/H0308","line":50},{"title":"House Bill 810","target":"https://legislature.idaho.gov/sessioninfo/2026/legislation/H0810","line":56},{"title":"House Bill 930","target":"https://legislature.idaho.gov/sessioninfo/2026/legislation/H0930","line":56},{"title":"Rep. Brent Crane, R-Nampa, opposes some proposed campaign finance reforms backed by fellow GOP member Secretary of State Phil McGrane.","target":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/public/latest-news/5r790z/picture285485472/alternates/FREE_1200/BOI_0213House19","line":64,"embedded":true}],"metadata":{"title":"Decades-old Idaho campaign finance laws remain on the books. Why reforms failed","source":"https://www.idahostatesman.com/news/politics-government/state-politics/article315317976.html?emci=8a4a98ea-9137-f111-8ef2-000d3a14b640&emdi=fd711587-f937-f111-8ef2-000d3a14b640&ceid=110103","author":["[[Kevin Fixler]]"],"published":"2026-04-13","created":"2026-07-07","description":"“If it ain’t broke, don’t fix it. And I can tell you, nothing’s broke with people raising money,” Nampa Republican Rep. Brent Crane said."},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},